{"id": 10008885, "reference": "A12/01010/23", "publication_date": "2023-05-02T15:53:30.810Z", "modification_date": "2023-05-02T15:53:30.812Z", "country": "Sweden", "product_category": "HOBBY_SPORTS_EQUIPMENT", "product_name": " Fish shaped pet toy ", "product_name_specific": "Toy for dogs and cats", "risk_description": "The cord has excessive concentrations of short chain chlorinated paraffins (SCCPs).\nSCCPs persist in the environment, are toxic to aquatic organisms at low concentrations and bio-accumulate in wildlife and humans, posing a risk to human health and the environment. Prolonged exposure to them through the skin may cause cancer. \nIn addition, the cord has excessive concentrations of bis(2-ethylhexyl) phthalate (DEHP), dibutyl phthalate (DBP) and lead (measured values up to 2.0 %, 3.7 %, 0.4 % and 0.13 % by weight, respectively). These phthalates may harm the health of children, possibly causing damage to their reproductive systems.\nThe solder in the product has excessive concentrations of lead and cadmium (measured values up to 82.2 % and 0.19 % by weight, respectively). \nLead and cadmium pose a risk to the environment.", "legal_provision": "The product does not comply with the requirements of the Directive on the restriction of the use of certain hazardous substances in electrical and electronic equipment (RoHS 2 Directive) nor with the Persistent Organic Pollutants (POP) Regulation.", "country_of_origin": "People's Republic of China", "sold_online": "NO", "notification_type": "ARTICLE_12", "brands": [], "model_types": [], "risk_types": ["CHEMICAL", "ENVIRONMENT"], "measures": ["PRODUCT_WITHDRAWAL_FROM_MARKET"], "embedding_model": "siglip2-b16-256", "embedding_dim": 768, "photos": [{"photo_id": 10080413, "main": true, "embedding": ""}, {"photo_id": 10080414, "main": false, "embedding": ""}, {"photo_id": 10080415, "main": false, "embedding": ""}]}